@startuml

title Secure Introduction: who trusts whom

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

package "platform" {
  [systemd, or an orchestrator] as launch
}

package "workload" {
  [a consumer,\nbefore any token] as wl
}

package "store" {
  [secret store] as vault
  database "registered public keys" as registry
}

package "issuer" {
  [token issuer] as idp
}

launch --> wl : delivers a key pair
launch ..> vault : the attestation it trusts
vault --> registry : looks the key up by name
wl <--> vault : challenge, answer,\nand the sealed secret
wl --> idp : obtains a token

legend bottom left
  /Platform integration/: the store verifies the platform's
  claim for the workload, as SPIFFE's node attestation does.
  /Trusted orchestrator/: an already-authenticated launcher
  injects one-of-a-kind material it can redeem once.
end legend

@enduml
